1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:05,821
OneNMRD Interface controls NMR
relaxometry experiments and

2
00:00:05,821 --> 00:00:08,707
analyses their NMRD profiles.

3
00:00:08,857 --> 00:00:12,525
It works with conventional and
fast-field-cycling consoles,

4
00:00:12,525 --> 00:00:14,119
in your web browser.

5
00:00:14,269 --> 00:00:19,274
Everything in this tour comes from its
built-in simulator: no hardware is moved.

6
00:00:20,774 --> 00:00:24,632
One interface drives different
consoles and magnets.

7
00:00:24,782 --> 00:00:28,893
FFC4, the fast-field-cycling
relaxometer at IST,

8
00:00:28,893 --> 00:00:32,926
runs on a Magritek Kea
console with Prospa.

9
00:00:33,076 --> 00:00:36,711
The Resonance Systems
ultraRelax8 runs through uSpin32,

10
00:00:36,711 --> 00:00:40,366
with generated run scripts
and its exported scans.

11
00:00:40,516 --> 00:00:45,375
The simulator stands in for either
console, for training and testing.

12
00:00:46,875 --> 00:00:51,947
Each console is chosen at the top,
with its own settings and hardware.

13
00:00:52,097 --> 00:00:55,886
On the ultraRelax8, the
field-cycling device levels,

14
00:00:55,886 --> 00:00:59,019
V1 and V2, come from
the field calibration,

15
00:00:59,019 --> 00:01:01,336
within the firmware limits.

16
00:01:02,836 --> 00:01:06,408
The sequences are field-cycling
and standard ones.

17
00:01:06,558 --> 00:01:08,416
Eight field-cycling sequences:

18
00:01:08,416 --> 00:01:11,699
polarised at high field or
starting from a low field,

19
00:01:11,699 --> 00:01:15,640
with inversion or saturation,
each also with a solid echo.

20
00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:20,578
Inversion recovery and saturation
recovery are the standard T1 sequences,

21
00:01:20,578 --> 00:01:23,223
at fixed field, on the ultraRelax8.

22
00:01:23,373 --> 00:01:27,744
RF tuning, and a Tune of any
sequence, come before the run.

23
00:01:29,244 --> 00:01:32,882
Each timing diagram is drawn from
the sequence's own pulse program,

24
00:01:32,882 --> 00:01:34,752
with the current parameters.

25
00:01:34,902 --> 00:01:36,813
It shows the field switching,

26
00:01:36,813 --> 00:01:39,054
the RF pulses and the acquisition;

27
00:01:39,054 --> 00:01:42,304
every segment opens the
parameter behind it.

28
00:01:42,454 --> 00:01:45,705
The plan lists temperature,
field, sequence,

29
00:01:45,705 --> 00:01:50,488
scans and τ values for each
row, and estimates the run time.

30
00:01:50,638 --> 00:01:54,035
Settings records which
sequences the hardware has.

31
00:01:55,535 --> 00:01:59,672
Run plan starts the experiment,
one row after another.

32
00:01:59,822 --> 00:02:04,324
Live acquisition shows every scan
as it arrives, with its spectrum.

33
00:02:04,474 --> 00:02:10,781
M is taken in the Mz window, with its σ,
the noise, and the signal-to-noise ratio.

34
00:02:10,931 --> 00:02:14,068
The average gets quieter
as the scans add up.

35
00:02:14,218 --> 00:02:18,145
M(τ) of the current field
builds up, point by point.

36
00:02:18,295 --> 00:02:21,988
When a field is complete, it
is fitted at once, with one,

37
00:02:21,988 --> 00:02:25,123
two or three exponentials,
in milliseconds.

38
00:02:25,273 --> 00:02:27,320
Meanwhile, Results follows the run:

39
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:31,647
each finished field can be looked
at while the next one is measured.

40
00:02:33,147 --> 00:02:35,874
The noise analysis is your choice.

41
00:02:36,024 --> 00:02:38,536
The phase treatment can
be phase independent,

42
00:02:38,536 --> 00:02:39,876
two-phase or four-phase,

43
00:02:39,876 --> 00:02:42,793
with the noise from the
scatter between scans.

44
00:02:42,943 --> 00:02:47,161
The previous Prospa analysis
stays available, for comparison.

45
00:02:47,311 --> 00:02:52,341
A Gaussian filter can be previewed
on the last scan before it is saved:

46
00:02:52,341 --> 00:02:53,191
here 20 kHz,

47
00:02:53,191 --> 00:02:57,438
with the filtered and unfiltered
averages side by side.

48
00:02:57,588 --> 00:02:58,907
On the ultraRelax8,

49
00:02:58,907 --> 00:03:03,908
a short noise and health check is
compared with the machine's reference,

50
00:03:03,908 --> 00:03:06,759
value by value, and kept as a trend.

51
00:03:08,259 --> 00:03:10,548
Diagnostics watches the magnet itself,

52
00:03:10,548 --> 00:03:13,560
through a planned field
monitor that only listens;

53
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,597
here the simulator plays it.

54
00:03:15,747 --> 00:03:18,630
It shows the Hall voltage
of the magnet supply live,

55
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:21,753
with the console's
field-switching pulses over it.

56
00:03:21,903 --> 00:03:24,738
Every switch is also
recorded at the full rate:

57
00:03:24,738 --> 00:03:27,755
here the last field-down
and field-up transitions,

58
00:03:27,755 --> 00:03:29,493
with the settling band.

59
00:03:29,643 --> 00:03:34,289
Each one is measured: delay,
rise and fall time, overshoot,

60
00:03:34,289 --> 00:03:39,521
settling time and pulse width,
as the last value and the mean.

61
00:03:39,671 --> 00:03:40,723
The field drift,

62
00:03:40,723 --> 00:03:44,867
the temperatures and the supply
rails show what changes slowly;

63
00:03:44,867 --> 00:03:47,519
lost data is flagged, never hidden.

64
00:03:47,669 --> 00:03:50,061
Every time comes from
the monitor's own clock,

65
00:03:50,061 --> 00:03:52,699
not from when the data
reached the computer.

66
00:03:54,199 --> 00:03:57,126
The final analysis is OneFit Engine's.

67
00:03:57,276 --> 00:04:00,267
Fit in OFE fits every field with OFE-Go,

68
00:04:00,267 --> 00:04:03,782
with MINOS errors and
reduced chi-square: here,

69
00:04:03,782 --> 00:04:06,599
four fields in about two seconds.

70
00:04:06,749 --> 00:04:08,643
The T1 dispersion is plotted,

71
00:04:08,643 --> 00:04:12,583
together with the T1 that
Prospa wrote, for comparison.

72
00:04:12,733 --> 00:04:17,100
The models are full OFE
expressions, and can be edited.

73
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:23,095
Open in OFE-GUI sends the
fit to a running OFE-GUI.

74
00:04:23,245 --> 00:04:26,770
It refits it and plots every
field, to change the model,

75
00:04:26,770 --> 00:04:29,009
the bounds or the plots there.

76
00:04:30,509 --> 00:04:35,069
The Terminal pane is a real shell
on the computer running OneNMRD,

77
00:04:35,069 --> 00:04:38,045
inside the page. It is off by default.

78
00:04:38,195 --> 00:04:42,832
Its Claude and Codex buttons start a
separately installed coding agent there,

79
00:04:42,832 --> 00:04:45,712
in a Docker sandbox when one is available.

80
00:04:45,862 --> 00:04:50,207
OneNMRD writes an AGENTS file
for them: how to reach the GUI,

81
00:04:50,207 --> 00:04:53,193
the hardware rules, and the JSON API.

82
00:04:53,343 --> 00:04:57,477
Here the API lists the
run and its four fields.

83
00:04:57,627 --> 00:05:01,259
A Tune or a Run asked for by an
agent waits for your Approve;

84
00:05:01,259 --> 00:05:02,978
Stop is always allowed.

85
00:05:04,478 --> 00:05:07,910
Plan, acquire, watch, and fit.

86
00:05:08,060 --> 00:05:12,522
OneNMRD Interface drives
FFC4 and the ultraRelax8,

87
00:05:12,522 --> 00:05:16,441
and hands the analysis to OneFit Engine.

88
00:05:16,591 --> 00:05:20,886
It is distributed under the
Artistic License 2.0. Prospa and

89
00:05:20,886 --> 00:05:23,033
uSpin32 are separate products,

90
00:05:23,033 --> 00:05:24,886
and are not included.
